  "description": "ThinkGeo.Cad is a layer extension to ThinkGeo.Core that lets you read CAD drawings and render them as a feature layer alongside the rest of your map. Built on the Open Design Alliance (\"ODA\") SDK v26.7.\n\nSupported formats (read):\n - AutoCAD: DWG, DXF\n - MicroStation: DGN\n - Autodesk: DWF\n\nCapabilities:\n - Render CAD drawings on a ThinkGeo map alongside vector and raster layers.\n - Reproject CAD coordinates on the fly to any spatial reference via PROJ.\n - Override CAD styling - colors, line widths, labels - through ThinkGeo.Core.\n\nTargets: .NET Framework 4.6.2+ and .NET Standard 2.1 (covers .NET Core 3.1, .NET 5 / 6 / 7 / 8 / 9).\nPlatforms: Windows x64 / x86 only. The bundled ODA SDK is Windows-native; CAD layers throw on Linux / macOS.\n\nDepends on ThinkGeo.Core. Pair with a UI package for your platform - see ThinkGeo.Core for the full list.\n\nCommercial product with a free 30-day evaluation. Sign up at https://helpdesk.thinkgeo.com/register and download ProductCenter to start.\n\nDocumentation: https://docs.thinkgeo.com/",
